# =============================================================================
# Simple Finance Multi-household — example environment configuration.
# Placeholders only. This repository is public: never add real identities,
# addresses, amounts or installation secrets here.
#
# Production: place at /data/.env in the new appdata root
#   /mnt/user/appdata/simple-finance-multi-household/.env
# This is a trusted, admin-owned (0600) file sourced by the container entrypoint.
# It must never be copied into the image or included in a household backup.
#
# The current source resolves finance storage from the verified registry
# assignment: households/<opaque-id>/simple-finance.sqlite and that household's
# documents/ directory. There are deliberately no DATABASE_PATH or
# DOCUMENTS_DIR overrides; never point this app at the original installation.
# See docs/MULTI_HOUSEHOLD_PLAN.md before changing storage or auth.
# =============================================================================

# --- Storage ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development data root (defaults to ./data); production container root is /data.
# DATA_DIR=./data
#
# Fixed household layout: /data/system/registry.sqlite and
# /data/households/<opaque-household-id>/{simple-finance.sqlite,documents/}.
# Household paths are derived from the active registry assignment, never env
# or request input. The old /data/simple-finance.sqlite is not selected.

# --- Authentication (Cloudflare Access) --------------------------------------
# Issuer: https://<your-team>.cloudflareaccess.com
# Audience: the Access application's AUD tag
# The app independently verifies the Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion JWT with jose.
# Cloudflare's email policy is the outer gate; in-app household assignment
# comes from the pre-provisioned system registry. A verified email that is
# not assigned to a household is denied (no self-sign-up).
# AUTH_ISSUER=
# AUTH_AUDIENCE=
# Optional override (defaults to $AUTH_ISSUER/cdn-cgi/access/certs):
# AUTH_CERTS_URL=
#
# Optional, read by the /admin "Server settings" panel only (issue #91):
# a bookmark link to the Cloudflare Access rule that controls sign-in.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCESS_URL=https://dash.cloudflare.com/<account>/access/apps
#
# OPTIONAL extra allowlist (legacy): anyone with an active assignment in the
# registry roster is allowed automatically — this list is only a fallback and
# can normally be left empty. Add an address here only if you want it to pass
# the allowlist WITHOUT a roster assignment (it will still be denied app
# access until it is assigned on /admin).
# AUTH_ALLOWED_EMAILS=alex@example.com,sam@example.com

# --- System registry (control plane) ------------------------------------------
# The registry at <DATA_DIR>/system/registry.sqlite holds the household roster,
# identity-to-household assignments and administrator roles — never finance
# records. Households and sign-in emails are managed in the app at /admin by a
# platform administrator.
#
# One-time bootstrap for a brand-new registry: while the roster is completely
# empty, the first app open creates REGISTRY_ADMIN_EMAIL's household and marks
# that identity as the platform administrator. Consumed once — the registry
# always keeps at least one administrator afterwards. The optional household
# name is operational metadata for the administrator's own household
# (default: "Main household").
#
# This address is also the only one that sees the Admin button in the app's
# menu, and the only one allowed to edit the Server settings panel on /admin
# (issue #91). If you ever change your own email address, edit both this line
# and the Cloudflare Access rule by hand, restart the container, sign in with
# the new address, and re-assign it to your household on /admin.
# REGISTRY_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# REGISTRY_ADMIN_HOUSEHOLD_NAME=

# --- Development identity (NEVER honoured in production) ---------------------
# Development bypass works only when AUTH_DEV_BYPASS=true, NODE_ENV is not
# production, and an identity is configured. It is for local development and
# Playwright only; it does not test Cloudflare or household assignment.
# AUTH_DEV_BYPASS=false
# AUTH_DEV_IDENTITY_EMAIL=dev@example.com

# --- Server -------------------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=3000

# --- Container only -----------------------------------------------------------
# Unraid defaults: 99 (nobody) and 100 (users). The new app maps host port 3009
# to container port 3000 and uses bridge networking.
# PUID=99
# PGID=100

# --- Cloudflare inspection and explicit email operations (issue #101) ------------------------------
# Server-side only; never paste tokens into chat or commit real values.
# Set in the trusted /data/.env or container environment and restart.
# Token: Account > Access: Apps and Policies > Read for inspection only;
# Edit (API name: Write) for explicit grants/removals, scoped to this account.
# Writes require a reusable Allow policy with app_count=1; see docs/CLOUDFLARE_INSPECTION.md.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# CLOUDFLARE_APPLICATION_ID=
# CLOUDFLARE_POLICY_ID=
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
